{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>You have troubled.</b> A term of troubled waters — my mind is not clear now (Berakhot 25). And the aggadah: the cask was clear and you troubled it (Bereshit Rabbah) — a tradition was in the hands of the Canaanites that they would fall by the hand of the sons of Jacob, but they would say, ״until it bears fruit and you inherit the land״ (Exodus 23) — therefore they were silent." "<b>Men of number.</b> Few people."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The citation (ברכות כ\"ה) likely refers to bBerakhot 25a, where the same idiom of troubled waters appears."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:06.050424052Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}